 ### Parameters and Edge Cases
-- **Image Resolution**: The visibility ordering is correct if the image resolution used for volume rendering is the same as the one used for computing the visibility ordering relations [S2, S3].
-- **Mesh Constraint**: The mesh must be acyclic [S2, S3].
-- **Geometry Constraint**: Cells may have nonplanar surfaces, provided their edges do not have projections that cross each other ("bow tie" quadrilateral projections) [S2, S3].
-- **Tiny Cells**: Tiny cells (those not projecting onto any screen pixels) may be output out of order if they are exterior cells, because the relationship $a <_{vp} b$ is only guaranteed if there is a continuous sequence of adjacent intervening cells [S2, S3]. Sorting sink cells by increasing distance of their centroid to the viewpoint reduces sorting errors for tiny exterior cells [S3].
-- **Splatting**: If splatting is used for antialiasing, sorting errors may occur for tiny cells because the relationship $a <_{vp} b$ is not guaranteed across regions where ray-gaps may occur [S3].
-- **Non-strict Ordering**: The sort may not be a strict visibility ordering if overlapping faces are not sampled at points in the region of overlap, though the image space ordering remains correct [S2, S3].
