 ## Subtopics
 
-### BSP-XMPVO
-An algorithm that improves XMPVO results by building a view-independent BSP tree of the exterior faces to reduce the number of ray shooting queries needed [S2]. It augments MPVO ordering using binary space partitions on boundary elements [S2]. Runtime is $O(n + bp)$, where $p$ is the size of a small subset of exterior cells [S2]. However, building the BSP structure is very slow, and the tree can become deep and unbalanced, leading to $O(b)$ cost per search and $O(b^2)$ overall flavor [S2]. Results are orders of magnitude better than previous exact methods, but SXMPVO is faster and easier to implement than BSP-XMPVO [S2, S3].
+### [BSP-XMPVO](1160-bsp-xmpvo.md)
+An algorithm that improves XMPVO results by building a view-independent BSP tree of the exterior faces to reduce the number of ray shooting queries needed. It augments MPVO ordering using binary space partitions on boundary elements. Runtime is $O(n + bp)$, where $p$ is the size of a small subset of exterior cells. However, building the BSP structure is very slow, and the tree can become deep and unbalanced, leading to $O(b)$ cost per search and $O(b^2)$ overall flavor. Results are orders of magnitude better than previous exact methods, but SXMPVO is faster and easier to implement than BSP-XMPVO.
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity**: $O(wh + a + n)$ for most data sets, where $w, h$ are image dimensions, $a$ is the projected area (pixels scanned), and $n$ is the number of cells [S2, S3]. Expected cost is $O(wh(\hat{d}_e + 1) + n)$, where $\hat{d}_e$ is the average depth complexity of exterior faces [S2, S3].
-- **Memory Complexity**: $O(wh + a)$ for A-Buffer, $O(a)$ for PN lists, $O(n)$ for PN list head pointers, and $O(b)$ for exterior face list [S2, S3].
-- **Performance**: On an SGI Power Onyx (R10000 250 MHz), for helix3.5 (3.57M cells, 375x450 image), SXMPVO uses 367 MB total vs MPVONC's 347.4 MB [S2, S3]. Sorting time for 1.5M cells is a linear function of projected exterior face area [S2]. On a 2.53 GHz Pentium 4, throughput is 500K-600K tetrahedra per second for a 1,050,000 pixel image [S2, S3].
-- **Strengths**: Faster than all published exact visibility ordering algorithms in object or image space [S2, S3]. Handles nonconvex boundaries, disconnected meshes, and mixed cell types [S2, S3]. No extra preprocessing compared to MPVO [S2, S3].
-- **Limitations**: Slower than MPVONC because it must determine and respect every relationship MPVONC does, plus exterior face relations [S3]. Requires acyclic meshes [S2, S3]. Tiny exterior cells may be out of order [S2, S3].
+- **Time Complexity**: $O(wh + a + n)$ for most data sets, where $w, h$ are image dimensions, $a$ is the projected area (pixels scanned), and $n$ is the number of cells [S2, S3, unofficial]. Expected cost is $O(wh(\hat{d}_e + 1) + n)$, where $\hat{d}_e$ is the average depth complexity of exterior faces [S2, S3, unofficial].
+- **Memory Complexity**: $O(wh + a)$ for A-Buffer, $O(a)$ for PN lists, $O(n)$ for PN list head pointers, and $O(b)$ for exterior face list [S2, S3, unofficial].
